1. Write a program that contains a string (char pointer) with a value ‘Hello world’. The program should XOR and AND each character in this string with 0 and 127, and display the result.
public class XorAnd {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String str = "Hello World";
        System.out.println("Original: " + str);
        System.out.print("XOR with 0: ");
        for (int i = 0; i < str.length(); i++) {
            System.out.print((char)(str.charAt(i) ^ 0));
        }
        System.out.print("\nAND with 127: ");
        for (int i = 0; i < str.length(); i++) {
            System.out.print((char)(str.charAt(i) & 127));
        }
    }
}
